#- §6╔═.✵.════════╗
 §5Join With The Unseen
§6╚════════.✵.═╝

     §5“ˢᵗᵃʳᵉ ᵃᵗ ᵗʰᵉ ᵈᵃʳᵏ 
      ᶠᵒʳ ᵗᵒᵒ ˡᵒⁿᵍ ᵃⁿᵈ 
    ʸᵒᵘ’ˡˡ ᵉᵛᵉⁿᵗᵘᵃˡˡʸ ˢᵉᵉ 
      ʷʰᵃᵗ ⁱˢⁿ’ᵗ ᵗʰᵉʳᵉ”

§8I stand alone in my magazine office. Well, not quite so alone anymore. I notice for the first time the dark
#- §8magic that has been pouring inside the room since day one. The place my eyes once saw as safe and as home, now feel distant and unfamiliar. I try to make sense of the sinister messages carved into the walls. The same ones that are now forever craved in my mind. Slowly walking inside 
#- §8the mailroom, I see green slime in the water cooler. I hope nobody has taken any.
A tiny floating creature snarls 
at me and uncharacteristically.....
I snarl back!
As I wander and take a seat at my desk, 
I hear the never-ending noises
that whisper to me
#- §8from another realm. Like voices trapped just a second out of sync with the rest of us. I catch a glimpse of my reflection on the computer screen. My face smiles back at me. But I am not the one smiling. It takes a moment for me to see that my face has changed on one side,
the once youthful 
#- §8floral features replaced by an unsettling mass of purple and black. Wide grinning teeth and a white hollow eye take a long look back at me, almost as surprised as I am. I exit the office and make my way downstairs to my beloved tavern; The Spyglass. The name that holds more 
#- §8meaning now, as the reality of my past begins to sink in. Once again I find myself noticing things that were not there before. I hear the piano still repeating ‘spooky scary skeletons’ with no bard in sight and think to myself how casually unbothered I was about that...
#- §8An impossible voice politely welcomes me and I look up to see an old version of myself from another lifetime, tending the bar. Looking around more I see evidence of successful and unsuccessful spell workings I've made previously. Remembering them triggers a spark 
#- §8inside me and I grow taller, my arms and legs painfully stretching unnaturally. I see purple specs all around me and rage floods my mind. The desire to attack is overwhelming but I somehow keep still. 
I yet again catch a reflection of myself 
in the window... 
#- §8I see an Enderman! The horror of an Enderman looking in 
its own eyes quickly turns me back. 

The tavern remains mostly untouched and holds its welcoming presence. I find comfort in this, until I recall that nobody has been here for a very long time...
#- §8In fact, I’ve seen very few people anywhere! This world has become a ghost town! Panic sets in, as I keep remembering all that has transpired. 
§0The Darkne…. 
    §5hₑllₒ 
           my     dₑₐᵣ 
§8A deep glitchy voice interrupts my thoughts. I feel scared yet relieved.  
#- §6It, you’re here!§5 
lₒₒkS lᵢkₑ ₒᵤᵣ lᵢTtlₑ plₐN wₒᵣKₑd! 

§8I take a closer look at my hands and body. §6Yes, I believe so, like we are one and the same! §8I hear laughter moving from one ear to the other, sending chills up my spine... 

§5tᵢll dₑₐtH      dₒ ᵤS pₐᵣt...
