#- §3╔═.⚓.════════╗
 §9A Hadean Fairy Tale
        By Mempo
§3╚════════.⚓.═╝
§1Eh, whaddya want? 
A scary story? 
Fine. Here ya go:

Millennia ago, a whole planet of creatures was just minding its own business, having a good time making hydrocarbons outta
#- §1the primordial ooze, you know, like ya do.

Then, §lwhabam!
§0§1In one little part of the vast shallow sea, somethin' new popped up. Maybe it was a mutation, maybe it was a space invader, maybe it was a monster from a parallel dimension.
§oWho knows...
#- §1But this little guy, he took all the good stuff outta the air and made it into a very toxic, very reactive gas. Deadly to everything else around it. Turned water inta acid, metal inta rust. Rock inta dirt.

And all around it, all the life around it
#- §1started dying. And this mutant monster, it ate up all the dead stuff and spread, and spread and spread, until the only place its predecessors could survive were the far edges of the world - the bottom of the oceans, the middle of deserts, sulfurous cracks in the earth.
It crowded out 
#- §1everyone and everything.

§oBut that wasn't the worst part.
§0
§1This poison gas got inta everything. Poison clouds, like big pillars in the air. Poison pools. Poison rain. 
The whole planetary atmosphere changed, and it started getting
#- §1colder and colder. Reflecting more sunlight, ya know?
Whole chunks of the ocean, froze solid. Magma cooled inta endless plains of black rock. And everything that ever was alive on this planet, every living thing, they died and died and died and died
and nothing could
#- §1stop it. Until the whole planet was nothing but big, roiling clouds of poison, poison winds blowing over a poison sea. And in it all, the invader, no doubt feelin' very pleased with itself, floating away in alla that poison, making more and more of it.
And that's the way it stayed. Forever.
#- §1What, you thought there was gonna be a different ending? Ferget it. The mutant organisms evolved into a whole poison biosphere, got multicellular after a while, split into animals and plants and fungi, and divided the whole world up. 
Yeah, I'm talking 
about you guys!
#- §1Ding-dang oxy-breathers.

But we old folks, hiding away in our deep-sea vents and sulphur pools? 

We remember. 
               Oh, we do...

And one day, we'll come back. And then you'll be sorry.
#- §6I'm sure i've heard 
at least 10 versions of that tale told 
at our tavern. 

Well, when people exisited that is...

