#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗           §2ᴛʜᴇ ᴇɴᴅ
§5╚════════.✵.═╝
§2Together Fern and Castien had found an End Portal. Something only ever spoken of as fiction and spooky tales to scare children. But in reality, those rumours scared everybody... 
They scared Fern most of all. 
#- §2Now standing alone hand in hand the two unlikely companions debate if this portal should be activated or kept a secret. 

The elf, out of his depth, tells the flower maiden gently; “§cI mean, we have to activate this right, because if we don’t, we’ll never know what The End is§2”.
#- §2“Trust me Cas, every petal in my body is telling me to take this leap of faith, but we have to consider that §5ɨȶ§2 is the one who brought us here”. 

Fern takes a deep breath and unsheathes her weapon. The sword she found as a child so very long ago. 
#- §2She taps on the cracked Ender Eye in the handle and then points towards the one empty portal frame where Castien retrieved his crown along with §5ɨȶ'ֆ §2note. The elf exhales sharply. “§cOh, I see§2”. “No… no you don’t see, nobody ever sees, only myself and §5ɨȶ§2 know the truth of
#- §2this world and the fates of all people who dwell here”. 

Fern begins to nervously pick at the Ender Eye attempting to take it out of the sword. “§cYou can tell me§2”. The elf speaks softly as he calmly takes the sword 
from Fern, noticing her unease.
#- §2“§cPlease tell me, a problem shared is a problem halved as they say§2”. Allowing Castien to take the sword away without hesitation, Fern rolls her eyes and says with years of built-up emotions “you won’t believe me”. The elf places the sword down on the floor and proceeds to sit on a
#- §2nearby rock... 
“§cTry me!§2” 

Fern shows a hint of a smile and sits down next to Castien. “Where do I even begin?” Fern says as she doubts herself. “§cTry the beginning§2” Castien says as he nudges Fern's shoulder. Fern nudges him back.
#- §2“Do you believe in past lives Cas?” “§cPast lives, well not really, I mean…§2”. Fern cuts him off. “Because everyone in Craftadia has them, all of them, even us, and every single time, §5ɨȶ§2 finds someone to attach to, someone powerful... chaos thrives and then §0The Darkness §2eventually comes, 
#- §2the whole world, darkness, erased, gone, reset, and nobody remembers, some do, yet never question it, but every time they carry on oblivious, they rebuild their lives again and again and again.”

Castien listens intensely trying hard not to interrupt.  
#- §2“I live so long, but I still remember all the versions of myself, past, present and future...” 
The elf holds his tongue no longer. “§cWhoa wait... remembering past lives is one thing but your future, how can that be possible?§2” Fern pauses for an uneasy length of time.
#- §2“§cCome back to me Fern, what are you thinking?§2” The elf and flower sit quietly in the small room. Tiny rocks falling from the roof reverberate through the long hallways of this forgotten fortress. Castien moves a small strand of hair off Fern's face and tucks it behind a leaf near
#- §2her ear. Fern is too focused on how she, §oor anyone for that matter,§0 §2could ever tell over 200 years worth of adventure... 

She picks up the sword from the floor and grabs the Ender Eye with one giant twist... 

letting the blade fall...
#- §2She stares into the eye and with a resentful tone of voice finally speaks;

§ktalkingtoyoutalkingtoyo
§0
§2“§oThe scars upon my back tell stories that no magazine has the spine to carry!§0§2”

§ktalkingtoyoutalkingtoyo
#- §2To be continued…
§5✿✿❀❀❀✿✿.✿✿❀❀❀✿✿

§2Tune in next time 
if there is more of... 
ꜰᴇʀɴ'ꜱ ᴀᴅᴠᴇɴᴛᴜʀᴇꜱ!

